<h2 local-id=3D"55064425f17b" id=3D"CloudPulse-AIOptimizer-Step1:Comprehens=
iveMetricsDiscoveryandFeatureRelevanceAnalysis"><strong><span data-colorid=
=3D"g9wcnhh0lb">Step 1: Comprehensive Metrics Discovery and Feature Relevan=
ce Analysis</span></strong></h2>
<p local-id=3D"03c1ff2688d3"><em>(keep your existing intro and the two sour=
ce sections =E2=80=94 Databricks System Tables / Databricks Cluster Logs =
=E2=80=94 unchanged)</em></p>
<p local-id=3D"b8f0d83116a7">Identifying Essential Metrics for the AI Recom=
mendation System</p>
<p local-id=3D"9c94990641cf"><em>(keep your existing 17-item list =E2=80=94=
 job_id through avg_total_shuffle_write_gb =E2=80=94 unchanged, then add:)<=
/em></p>
<p local-id=3D"fe4e4e9775f5">Additional signals specifically powering the <=
strong>serverless-viability scoring model</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"09c5efe5-8675-43bc-b3b0-bfcf43c90ef1">
<li local-id=3D"aaaa4e84-b3e5-425d-8ba6-aadfa7127224">
<p local-id=3D"28fdd7adf235"><strong>avg_total_dis_used_gb</strong> =E2=80=
=93 Disk spill volume. Serverless compute has no local disk, so any spill i=
s treated as a hard disqualifier for migration.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c7831aa3-cdd3-4720-8ea8-9044f02febdf">
<p local-id=3D"d7b19b0de43f"><strong>avg_total_input_gb</strong> =E2=80=93 =
Input data volume, used to normalize shuffle/spill intensity per job.</p></=
li>
<li local-id=3D"197b2f4d-66cb-459d-8d6b-82c5f03a17da">
<p local-id=3D"c8ad98e75b97"><strong>ttl_exec_idle_pct</strong> =E2=80=93 E=
xecutor idle percentage, a core signal for how much a job would benefit fro=
m serverless elasticity.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4dc23945-ca67-40f9-8d5d-037a516fa5ae">
<p local-id=3D"dedc2a49de71"><strong>avg_setup_dur_sec</strong> =E2=80=93 C=
luster startup/setup duration, used to compute startup-latency ratio agains=
t runtime.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"c93398be-377d-46ce-8dd0-7c9ba9a0fb98">
<p local-id=3D"869f5cba23cd"><strong>ttl_exec_add_count / ttl_exec_remove_c=
ount</strong> =E2=80=93 Executor churn (autoscaling add/remove events per r=
un), indicating burstiness.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b69db792-ed90-4419-a89a-cee42904724c">
<p local-id=3D"d35245a04495"><strong>avg_max_single_task_duration_sec / avg=
_tasks_cnt / avg_total_tasks_time_sec</strong> =E2=80=93 Task-level skew si=
gnals used in risk scoring.</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"96f67f1bd009"><strong>Step 2: ETL Framework for Dataset Gene=
ration</strong></p>
<p local-id=3D"b5566e13a609"><em>(unchanged =E2=80=94 your description of t=
he pipeline stages and output tables matches the notebooks exactly: </em><c=
ode>dxm_run_level_exec_stats_log</code><em>, </em><code>dxm_run_level_sys_s=
tats</code><em>, </em><code>dxm_run_level_stats_log</code><em>, </em><code>=
job_level_stats</code><em>. Optionally add one line noting two supporting u=
tilities not otherwise mentioned: a static config-drift scanner that flags =
runtime Spark config overrides invisible to cluster-boot logs, and a task-a=
ttribution step that resolves stage/SQL-plan stats to individual tasks in m=
ulti-task jobs.)</em></p>
<h2 local-id=3D"7022720c833b" id=3D"CloudPulse-AIOptimizer-Step3:AI-DrivenR=
ecommendationGeneration"><strong><span data-colorid=3D"utaz10li9q">Step 3: =
AI-Driven Recommendation Generation</span></strong></h2>
<p local-id=3D"8adc69cdd16f">Once the curated and fully engineered dataset =
is prepared, recommendations are generated through a <strong>hybrid engine<=
/strong> that combines deterministic scoring with AI-driven reasoning =E2=
=80=94 not a single end-to-end AI call.</p>
<p local-id=3D"458fbe3e9509"><em>Cluster right-sizing</em> (node type and a=
utoscaling range adjustments) is generated directly by the AI model, which =
analyses CPU, memory, and GC utilization signals against the node specifica=
tion catalog for each job.</p>
<p local-id=3D"0983c376d6af"><em>Serverless viability</em> is computed diff=
erently and more conservatively, since it carries direct cost and reliabili=
ty risk if wrong:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"674e5c6c-5009-4cd2-b933-9b2fe5a38544">
<li local-id=3D"bacc15d7-dd24-45f5-8ecb-07ce1935bb8c">
<p local-id=3D"6b6c05ae3531">A deterministic scoring formula (computed upst=
ream in the ETL pipeline, not by the AI) produces an <code>infra_benefit_sc=
ore</code>, <code>risk_score</code>, and combined <code>serverless_score</c=
ode> for every job, weighting factors like burstiness, idle waste, start-up=
 latency, shuffle intensity, disk spill, GC pressure, and task skew.</p></l=
i>
<li local-id=3D"08bd8989-f4e2-4b22-a85e-acfef750ab6d">
<p local-id=3D"ba4fc5f68e89">The AI model's role is constrained to <strong>=
explaining and, in ambiguous cases, adjusting that score by exactly one ste=
p</strong> =E2=80=94 it cannot override a hard disqualifier (e.g., any disk=
 spill), and it can never upgrade a "Not Recommended" job straight to "Reco=
mmended."</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e48d95ae-257d-48a0-85b3-b4a38d047bd4">
<p local-id=3D"60e56d51fba6">If the AI call fails for any reason, the syste=
m falls back to the deterministic score rather than blocking the recommenda=
tion.</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"359744314924">This hybrid design is what keeps outputs consi=
stent, interpretable, and resistant to hallucination =E2=80=94 the AI layer=
 is advisory, not authoritative, over decisions with direct cost impact.</p=
>
<p local-id=3D"7a0f63acfe19">Recommendation outputs include:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"48005c88-9069-43ad-b691-193709451809">
<li local-id=3D"99b7bb3d-cf43-4775-a3ca-c0d36bbfca4e">
<p local-id=3D"d4e00868ead2">Recommended node type adjustments</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1d73e82f-6284-4fc8-ae70-e1a828433cf9">
<p local-id=3D"c02729c948bb">Optimized autoscaling ranges</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"34d9cfc6-fcae-4cc9-9f43-e712d41aafa1">
<p local-id=3D"87d52307f895">Serverless viability checks with explainable r=
easoning</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"63a37aaf-0aee-49be-99ac-10733c3936f1">
<p local-id=3D"d6765739b750">Cost-efficiency improvement opportunities</p><=
/li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"427a07294dd6" id=3D"CloudPulse-AIOptimizer-Step4:Integratio=
nwithDatabricksApps(CloudPulseUI)"><strong><span data-colorid=3D"pmrllwpc9m=
">Step 4: Integration with Databricks Apps (Cloud Pulse UI)</span></strong>=
</h2>
<p local-id=3D"3e8ccd14d124">The final stage delivers the AI-generated insi=
ghts through an intuitive and interactive interface within the Cloud Pulse =
Databricks App. This UI enables users to seamlessly consume, interpret, and=
 act on the recommendations. It provides:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"dccdb209-e14a-41f9-8400-175c09b7135e">
<li local-id=3D"569c1316-0974-4848-afd1-1e3e1603b9ef">
<p local-id=3D"a186117d857c">Clear job-level configuration recommendations<=
/p></li>
<li local-id=3D"44a9d754-ded7-478c-8423-27ad1ca4f6fb">
<p local-id=3D"1ddacbd24313">Visual indicators of performance and cost inef=
ficiencies</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1e1c1ee2-9bc3-4e7f-9287-eafe9e766219">
<p local-id=3D"9bfe47c848f9">Actionable insights presented in an accessible=
, user-friendly format</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"1292024a5455">Beyond the baseline recommendations, the inter=
face also surfaces advanced operational intelligence, including:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"af7f86dc-2215-4684-92ca-47404017b8ff">
<li local-id=3D"53b64f35-f6c5-4517-94d7-7a74c9e7801a">
<p local-id=3D"36e2e7773503"><strong>Serverless viability evaluations</stro=
ng> for each job, accompanied by detailed justification</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4ea89718-b185-4fea-9879-201cc4831163">
<p local-id=3D"701a3448f68e"><strong>Provisioning assessments</strong> to i=
dentify whether jobs are under-provisioned, over-provisioned, or appropriat=
ely sized, with contextual reasoning</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"feaced290791">The dashboard further highlights key financial=
 and optimization metrics:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"29ef0861-058b-4fce-b658-6649651f54ae">
<li local-id=3D"f756eab1-82bf-4fbc-acfb-2cda493658aa">
<p local-id=3D"bdc39baf1a6b"><strong>Top 10 most expensive jobs</strong>, i=
ncluding current vs. projected cost and estimated annual savings</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e0a47396-52b5-4b77-910f-0c0dd66c2637">
<p local-id=3D"73bf0786cc71"><strong>DBU consumption comparison</strong> (c=
urrent vs. optimized), with potential annual DBU reductions</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5eadd8fb-835a-4f97-8738-0f7de3507462">
<p local-id=3D"d8f123d22ec8"><strong>Optimization progress metrics</strong>=
, showing how many jobs have been optimized and how many remain</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7f3cf970-e3f5-40fb-9627-79f89ed76e1c">
<p local-id=3D"47f783f3e97b"><strong>Overall improvement percentages</stron=
g> resulting from the recommended configurations</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"14d233e76387">This integration ensures that insights are not=
 only generated by the AI engine but are effectively surfaced and operation=
alized, driving real-world optimization across teams and workloads.<br></p>
